STEP Greek
Version 3.0b1

December 5, 2020
Daniel Benjamin Miller <dbmiller@dbmiller.org>

This is a beta version of the STEP Greek font. Only a regular face is available
at present, though there are plans to add italic, bold and bold italic in the
future. The font only supports LGR in TeX and is meant to serve as a Greek
complement to a Times-like font such as STEP. The font supports polytonic
Greek.

STEP Greek is released under the SIL Open Font License; see STEP-COPYING.

For use, simply set the font as \rmdefault (if your document is all in LGR),
or, preferably, use substitutefont with babel:

\usepackage{substitutefont}
\substitutefont{LGR}{\rmdefault}{STEPGreekTest-TLF}
